WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.850
In acid solution, propanone
reacts with bromine.

2
00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:08.510
Double the concentration of propanone,
and the reaction goes twice as fast.

3
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.510
Double the bromine, though,
and nothing changes.

4
00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.270
The rate stays exactly the same.

5
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.150
Bromine is one of the reactants.

6
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.530
So why doesn't adding more
of it speed up the reaction?

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.070
In this mission, you'll break
reactions into elementary steps,

8
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:27.010
and meet intermediates, transition
states and molecularity.

9
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.690
You'll find out how a mechanism
sets the rate equation,

10
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:35.130
and read the energy profile of a
reaction with more than one step.

11
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:39.550
Your mission: explain why more
bromine doesn't speed up the reaction.
